  "plan": {
    "goal": "Culture human proximal tubular epithelial cells (PTECs) in a microchannel under apical fluid shear stress matching the physiological range of the human proximal tubule.",
    "rationale": "Human proximal tubule apical fluid shear stress is reported in the literature at ~0.2–1.0 dyn/cm² (0.02–0.1 Pa), with ~0.5 dyn/cm² (0.05 Pa) a commonly used representative value. I targeted 0.05 Pa. Using a standard OOC channel (400 µm wide × 100 µm high), the flow_rate_for_shear_stress calculator gives 2 µL/min to achieve 0.05 Pa (medium viscosity 1e-3 Pa·s). Verification: wall shear = 0.05 Pa, Re ≈ 0.13 (laminar), pressure drop ≈ 20 Pa (negligible), residence time ≈ 24 s. PTECs are not in the physiology registry, so the shear target is literature-based and should be confirmed against the specific PTEC line used.",
